		document D24
		note {
			value """
Comments on "Everything You Every Wanted to Know about GEDCOM Tags" SOURCE Record.

This is a set of notes about this SOURCE record. These notes are for anything else needed. There are other places to enter notes about the storage of the source (in the Repository link) and about the data in the source (in the DATA structure).

This particular SOURCE record uses all possible GEDCOM tags for a SOURCE record. Some things to check are:

1. Are the separate notes structures in the Repository link and the DATA structure preserved on importing?

2. Does the software recognize two sets of event types in the DATA structure?

3. Are the multimedia links preserved?

4. This record as two sets of notes - this one in a separate record and a second one embedded in the SOURCE record. Are they both imported and kept separate?"""
